# Build context for apps/server/Dockerfile ONLY. BuildKit prefers `<Dockerfile>.dockerignore`
# over the root `/.dockerignore`, and that root file is NOT shareable here on purpose: its
# `!packages/…` lines are pinned by a workspace test to be EXACTLY the organizer's compile
# closure, so admitting `packages/services`/`packages/api` there would either break that
# guard or, worse, quietly widen the organizer's boundary. Two images, two closures, two
# allow-lists.
#
# Same discipline as the root file: DENY EVERYTHING, RE-ADMIT THE BUILD'S INPUTS. This host's
# closure is core, db, db-mail (via db), services and api — an import reaching outside it
# resolves to a workspace link whose target holds only a manifest, and the bundle FAILS to
# build.
*

# Workspace manifests and the pinned resolution — `npm ci` validates the lockfile against
# every workspace manifest it finds.
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!apps/*/package.json
!packages/*/package.json

# The build steps the image runs: the host bundler and the esbuild loader it shares with the
# engine build (the version pin lives there).
!scripts/bundle-host.mjs
!scripts/engine-bundle.mjs

!apps/server
!packages/core
!packages/db
!packages/db-mail
!packages/services
!packages/api

# …minus anything inside them that must never be copied in: no test trees, no stale local
# compile output, no previous bundle run.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.DS_Store
**/.claude
**/test

# Secrets never enter an image layer; every value arrives as a compose/service variable.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
